// Test: bugfixes/validator_min_value_is_not_a_function
// Grammar: function_call (validator.minValue)
// Semantic: FUNC001 — stdlib-reference §15 has no `validator.minValue` /
//   `validator.maxValue`; numeric bounds are `validator.range(v, lo, hi)`
//   (developer decision)
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   error[FUNC001]
//   Function 'validator.minValue' not found
//   Use validator.range(v, lo, hi) for numeric bounds
//
// Regression: validator.minValue / validator.maxValue compiled though §15
// does not have them: an undeclared validator.* call was not checked at all.

start:
	integer v = validator.field(validator.create(), "age")
	v = validator.minValue(v, 13)
	print(validator.isOk(validator.run(v, 0)))
